From 8d303f03b82837d23ba32918ad7a8cced94320e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:37:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] e-ink: sleep screen weather and event as a centred footer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The two corners looked unordered (two stacks of different sizes, no
shared baseline, an icon drawn in a padded square), and every boxed or
columned layout tried after them looked busier than the clock above.
The simplest one won: two centred lines at the bottom, one size, one
weight, on the clock's axis:

    Berlin · [icon] 5°C · Cloudy
    Tomorrow 19:30 · Eat candy

- Each item is one line and never wraps. On the weather line a long
  city name is shortened first, so the temperature and the condition
  ("Cloudy", in the phone's language, from HiBreakParts) stay; on the
  event line the title is shortened, the time never is. With only one
  of the two, it takes the bottom line.
- The icon sits inline, centred on the capital height; EinkWeatherIcon
  places icons by their ink with the same line width for all of them.
- Tunable: debug.sysui.eink_sleep.footer_{size,leading,icon}.
- hibreak_sleep_weather_data version 2 adds the WMO code and the
  condition; version 1 still reads.
